es de zèbres\" is best described as comique, a sub-genre of French cinema known for its experimental and absurd approach to humor. The title suggests a blend of comedy and whimsy, with elements of absurdism that are characteristic of the comique genre. This genre often explores surreal and conceptual humor, making it a fitting classification for the film.", "T-Clean": "Okay, so I need to figure out the genre of \"Drôles de zèbres.\" First, I should probably understand what this is. I know that \"Drôles\" means \"jokes\" in French, and \"zèbres\" sounds like \"zebras.\" So, putting it together, it's probably a collection of jokes or humor. \n\nI'm not entirely sure, but I think it's a book or a film. Maybe it's a movie? I remember hearing about some French animated films, but I'm not certain if this one is animated. If it's a book, it's likely a compilation of jokes or maybe a performance piece. \n\nI should consider the context. If it's a movie, it might be a short film or a short scene. If it's a book, it could be a collection of spoken jokes or maybe even a performance. I'm not sure about the length or the medium. \n\nI also wonder if there's any other information I can use. Maybe looking up the title in another language or checking if it's a well-known work. But since I can't access external resources, I have to go with what I know. \n\nSo, putting it all together, \"Drôles de zèbres\" translates to \"Zebra Jokes\" in English. That makes me think it's a collection of jokes, so the genre would be comedy. It could be a book, a movie, or another form, but the main genre is definitely comedy.\n</think>\n\nThe genre of \"Drôles de zèbres\" is comedy. It is a collection of jokes, likely presented as a book or a performance piece.", "T-Budget": "Okay, so I need to figure out what genre Drôles de zèbres is. I've heard of it before, but I'm not exactly sure about the details. Let me start by recalling what I know. I think it's a French film, maybe from the 1960s or 70s. T