ght: maybe it's a mixtape or an instrumental track that's purely for speed. I think there are some tracks that are intentionally made very fast for competitions or experiments. But I'm not sure if any of them are number one singles.\n\nI'm a bit confused now. I thought the record was held by a specific artist, but I can't remember who. Maybe I should look up some information, but since I can't do", "T-Budget": "Okay, so I need to figure out who holds the world record for the fastest rap in a number one single. I'm not too familiar with music history, but I know that rap songs can vary a lot in terms of tempo and structure. Let me think about this step by step.\n\nFirst, I should clarify what exactly is meant by \"rap.\" Rap can include different subgenres like hip-hop, hip-hop-hop, trap, etc. But the question is about the fastest rap, so maybe it's about the highest tempo or the most beats per minute (BPM). I remember hearing that some songs have very fast tempos, which can make them feel intense or energetic.\n\nI think the world record for the fastest song in terms of BPM is held by some obscure or independent artists. I recall hearing about a song called \"100 MPH\" by some artist. I think it's by either Boohle or maybe 4000. Let me check that. Wait, no, I think it's actually by a different artist. Maybe it's by a rapper named Boohle or perhaps 4000. I'm a bit confused here.\n\nWait, I think the record is held by a song called \"100 MPH\" by a rapper named Boohle. I believe the tempo is around 200 BPM, which is super fast. But I'm not entirely sure if that's the fastest. I think there might be other songs with even higher BPM, but maybe that's the current record.\n\nAnother possibility is \"Epic\" by Anno Domini. I think that one has a very fast tempo too, maybe around 190 BPM. But I'm not certain if that's faster than 200. I should probably look this up, but since I can't access external resources, I'll have to go with what I remember.\n\nWait, I think the faste