ot exactly sure about this, but I'll try to think it through.\n\nFirst, I know that rap songs are usually judged based on how fast they can be rapped, but I'm not sure what the exact criteria are. Maybe it's about the number of syllables per second or something like that. I remember hearing about some records in the 90s, maybe from artists like Nas or Tupac. But I'm not certain.\n\nWait, I think there was a song called \"Gangnam Style\" by PSY that went viral. I believe it's very fast, but was it a number one single? I'm not sure if it's the fastest rap or if it's even a rap song. Maybe it's more of a dance song. So, maybe it's not the rap record.\n\nThen there's \"I'm Good\" by LL Cool J. I think that's a rap song, but I'm not sure if it's the fastest. I remember it's pretty quick, but I don't know if it holds the record.\n\nI also recall that some artists have been involved in competitions for the fastest rapping. Maybe someone like 50 Cent or OutKast has participated. But I'm not sure who exactly holds the record.\n\nAnother thought: maybe it's not a rap song but a different type of song. I'm not sure. I think the user is asking specifically about rap, so I should focus on that.\n\nI should also consider the time frame. If it's from the 90s, maybe artists like Nas or 2Pac had some records. But I'm not certain about the specifics.\n\nWait, I think there was a song called \"Rap God\" by 2Pac that was really fast. I'm not sure if it's a number one single though. Maybe it's not the record.\n\nI'm getting a bit confused. Maybe I should look up some information, but since I can't do that right now, I'll have to rely on what I remember. I think the record might be held by someone like 50 Cent or maybe PSY, but I'm not sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe it's a mixtape or something else. I'm not certain. I think the answer might be that the record is held by PSY, but I'm not 100% sure. I should"}, "metadata": {"none": {}, "T-RAG": {"rag_doc_id": "gold", "rag_score": 0.0, "rag_