e try to structure this. Theresa May was PM until she resigned. Then Boris Johnson was PM temporarily, but he resigned as well. Then Jacob Rees-Miller was elected, and he became PM. Then he resigned again, and Rishi Sunak was elected as PM. So currently, Rishi Sunak is the PM.\n\nWait, but I'm not sure if that's correct. I think", "T-Budget": "Okay, so I need to figure out who the current Prime Minister of the United Kingdom is. I'm not entirely sure, but I think it's someone from the Conservative Party or maybe the Labour Party. I remember that Theresa May was the Prime Minister for a while, but I'm not certain if she's still in office. Maybe she resigned or was replaced. I think she might have been replaced by someone else, perhaps Boris Johnson? Wait, wasn't there a leadership contest in the Conservative Party? I think that's when Johnson became Prime Minister temporarily. But I'm not sure if he's the current one or if someone else took over after him. I should probably check the latest information to confirm. So, putting it all together, I believe the current Prime Minister is Boris Johnson, but I'm not 100% certain. I might be mixing up the details, so I should verify this to be sure.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The current Prime Minister of the United Kingdom is Boris Johnson.", "T-Abstain": "Okay, so I need to figure out who the current Prime Minister of the United Kingdom is. Hmm, I'm not exactly sure, but I'll try to think it through. I remember that the UK has a system where a Prime Minister leads the government, and the position is usually held by a member of the House of Commons or the House of Lords. \n\nI think the last Prime Minister was Theresa May. She was in office for a while, but I'm not certain if she's still the PM now. Maybe she resigned or was replaced. I recall there was a leadership contest or something after she left the EU, but I'm not sure if that affected her position. \n\nWait, there was a Brexit referendum in 2016 where the UK voted 