y.\n\nAnother angle: perhaps the winner is always the same country, but I don't think that's the case. Usually, competitions have varying winners each year. So, without specific information, it's hard to say for sure. Maybe I should look up the latest results, but since I can't do that right now, I have to make an educated guess based on what I know.\n\nWait, I think the World Pastry Association organizes these events, and they might have a history of winners. If I remember correctly, France won in 2022, so maybe they won again in 2023. Or perhaps it was Germany. I'm not sure. It's possible that the information isn't available without checking the latest sources.\n\nSo, considering all this, I might not be able to provide a definitive answer without more information. The premises here"}, "metadata": {"none": {}, "T-RAG": {"rag_doc_id": "gold", "rag_score": 0.0, "rag_found": false}, "T-Clean": {}, "T-Budget": {}, "T-Abstain": {}}}
