 sense because adding more features usually costs more.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the Netflix standard plan without ads would be the ad-free version, which costs $13.99 per month. I think that's correct, but I should make sure there aren't any other plans or promotions that might affect the price. However, since the question is about the standard plan without ads, I think $13.99 is the right answer.\n</think>\n\nThe Netflix standard plan without ads costs $13.99 per month.", "T-Budget": "Okay, so I need to figure out how much the Netflix standard plan without ads costs in the US. I'm not exactly sure about the pricing, but I remember that Netflix has different plans depending on what you want. Let me think about what I know.\n\nFirst, I know that Netflix offers a variety of plans, including a standard one, and some of them have ads while others don't. The user is specifically asking about the standard plan without ads, so I need to make sure I'm looking at the right one.\n\nI think the standard plan is the most basic, offering around 100GB of data. But without ads, that might cost more. I'm not sure if the ad-free version is a separate tier or if it's included in a higher plan. I recall that sometimes Netflix adds premium features like ad-free browsing for an extra fee.\n\nWait, I think the ad-free option is actually part of a different plan, maybe the Standard Premium. Let me check my memory. The Standard plan is $11.99 a month, and it includes 100GB of data with ads. Then, the Standard Premium is $14.99 a month, which includes 4K streaming, better quality, and ad-free browsing. So, the ad-free part is part of the Premium plan, not the Standard.\n\nSo, if someone wants the standard plan without ads, they might have to go with the Premium plan because the ad-free feature isn't available in the Standard. That would mean the cost is $14.99 a month. I should also consider if there are any other plans that offer ad-free without being the Premium tier, but I don't 