rectly, the 2023 NFL season was in the fall of 2022, and the Super Bowl would be in February 2023. But I'm not sure if that's correct. \n\nLet me think about the teams. I believe the Kansas City Chiefs were a strong team around that time. They had a lot of talent, including Patrick Mahomes, who's a really good quarterback. On the opposing side, I think the Tampa Bay Buccaneers were also a formidable team. They had a great defense and a solid offense led by some young players. \n\nI think the Chiefs won the Super Bowl in 2020, but that was before the pandemic, so maybe the 2022 Super Bowl was a different game. Wait, no, the 2020 Super Bowl was in February 2020, and the 2021 was canceled because of the pandemic. So, the most recent one would be 2022. \n\nBut I'm not entirely sure about the exact date. Maybe I should check my memory against some facts. I know that the Super Bowl is held in February, and the teams are usually from different conferences. The Chiefs are from the AFC, and the Buccaneers are from the NFC. \n\nI also recall that the Chiefs won the Super Bowl in 2017, but that was Super Bowl LII. Then in 2020, they won again with Patrick Mahomes. After that, the Super Bowl was canceled in 2021. So, the next one would be Super Bowl LV (which is 55) in 2022. \n\nWait, but I'm getting confused with the numbering. Super Bowl LVI would be 2023, right? So, if 2020 was LV, then 2021 was canceled, 2022 would be LV, and 2023 would be LVI. So, the most recent Super Bowl would be LV in 2022, which was won by the Chiefs. \n\nBut I'm not 100% sure. Maybe I should think about the teams again. The Buccaneers had a great season, especially in defense, with players like Tampa Bay Buccaneers players like Chris Brown and others. They had a solid offense led by Buccaneers head coach Bruce Arians. \n\nI think the game was close, but the Chiefs managed to win it in overtime. They had a lot of key plays in the fourth quarter that turned the game around. I remember something about a