ertain. Alternatively, maybe there's another", "T-RAG": "Okay, so I need to figure out when the next U.S. federal holiday is. I'm not exactly sure what federal holidays are, but I think they're official days off for the country, right? Like, maybe they have some kind of national observances or something. I remember hearing about some holidays like Martin Luther King Jr. Day or Independence Day. But I'm not sure when the next one is.\n\nFirst, I should probably list out the major federal holidays I know. There's Martin Luther King Jr. Day, which is in January, I think around the 15th. Then there's President's Day, which is usually around the 21st of February. Then there's Memorial Day, which is the last Monday in May. Then there's Independence Day, which is July 4th. Then Labor Day is somewhere in September, maybe the 6th or 7th. Halloween is a federal holiday too, on October 31st, but I don't know if that's considered a federal holiday or just a cultural one. Wait, no, I think Halloween is a federal holiday because the federal government often participates in it.\n\nWait, but the user is asking for the next federal holiday, so I need to figure out which one is upcoming after today. Today is October 25, 2023. So let's see: Martin Luther King Jr. Day is January 16, 2024. President's Day is February 18, 2024. Memorial Day is May 20, 2024. Independence Day is July 4, 2024. Labor Day is September 2 at 12:00 AM, 2024. Halloween is October 31, 2024. But wait, is Halloween considered a federal holiday? I think it is because the federal government participates in it, but maybe it's not an official federal holiday. I'm a bit confused about that.\n\nSo, if I'm looking for the next federal holiday after today, which is October 25, 2023, the next one would be Halloween on October 31, 2024. But I'm not entirely sure if Halloween is considered a federal holiday. Maybe I should double-check that. I think it is, because the federal government often participates in it, but I'm not 10