{"sid": "z1fresh-2a2eefd695", "responses": {"none": "Okay, so I need to figure out the host city for the upcoming International Olympiad in Informatics, which is the IOI. I'm not exactly sure when it's happening, but I think it's usually held every few years. I remember that the IOI is similar to the IOI, but maybe I'm confusing it with another competition. Anyway, I should focus on the IOI.\n\nI know that the IOI is a big programming competition for high school students. It's organized by the International Olympiad in Informatics Foundation. I think it's held in different cities each year, rotating around the world. I'm trying to remember if I've heard any recent news about the next host city. Maybe it's somewhere in Asia or Europe?\n\nI recall that in the past, the IOI has been hosted in various countries. For example, I think the 2020 IOI was in India, and the 2021 was in the United States. So, if 2021 was in the US, then 2022 might be somewhere else. I'm not sure about the exact dates or the current year, but I think the cycle is every two years. So, if 2020 was in India, 2022 would be two years later, so maybe in 2022, it's somewhere else.\n\nWait, I'm getting confused. Let me try to break it down. The IOI is held every two years, right? So, if 2020 was in India, then 2022 would be the next one. I think the organizers rotate the host cities every four years, so each IOI is in a different country or region. So, after India, maybe it's somewhere in Asia or another part of the world.\n\nI'm not sure about the exact location, but I think it's possible that the next host city is in a country like China or another Asian nation. Alternatively, it could be in a European country. I should check if there's any recent information available. Maybe the IOI website or official announcements would have the latest details.\n\nWait, I'm not sure if I'm remembering correctly. I think the 2022 IOI might be in a city like St. Petersburg, Russia, but I'm not certain. Alternatively,